#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities.rst:5
msgid "DisplayPort Link Capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:24
msgid ""
"The Intel DP link caps API tracks the supported and allowed DisplayPort link "
"configurations for a DP encoder and its attached connectors, and provides "
"helpers to iterate over the allowed configurations and constrain them by "
"filtering, disabling, or limiting them to maximum link parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:33
msgid ""
"All accesses to this API must be serialized. The only exception is "
"intel_dp_link_caps_get_max_limits(), which allow lockless lookup. Such "
"lookups may observe an out-of-sync :c:type:`struct intel_dp_link_config "
"<intel_dp_link_config>` tuple, i.e. a rate from one state and a lane count "
"from another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:39
msgid ""
"The Intel i915/xe drivers ensure the above serialization by holding :c:type:"
"`drm_mode_config.connection_mutex <drm_mode_config>` and, while holding the "
"lock, waiting for any pending asynchronous atomic commits. This also allows "
"use of the API from the tails of asynchronous atomic commits, which cannot "
"hold the lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:48
msgid ""
"The link configuration iterators can iterate the ``allowed configurations`` "
"during modeset configuration selection or link training fallback handling in "
"a configurable order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:52
msgid ""
"The iteration order can depend on connector type (eDP, DP SST, DP MST) and "
"modeset-specific conditions or driver policies, such as DSC vs. non-DSC "
"modes, power saving vs. better user experience, or policy changes after a "
"link training failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:57
msgid ""
"The configurations exposed via the iterators can be additionally constrained "
"in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:60
msgid ""
"Filtered for a given modeset based on modeset-specific conditions. Examples "
"for such conditions include driver policies preferring power saving or "
"better user experience, post-link training failure preference changes, or "
"sink automated test requests limiting the usable configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:66
msgid ""
"Disabled permanently for the connected sink. Examples of reasons to disable "
"a configuration include a link training failure for a given configuration or "
"a driver workaround preventing the use of a particular configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:71
msgid ""
"Limited via a maximum link rate and lane count. For example, after a link "
"training failure, subsequent modesets may be limited to configurations at or "
"below the failed parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:75
msgid ""
"This mechanism exists for backward compatibility only. Eventually, it will "
"be removed in favor of relying solely on individually disabled "
"configurations, as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:82
msgid ""
"``Common link capabilities`` (or ``common caps``) refer to the link rates "
"and maximum lane count supported by both the source and the sink, i.e. the "
"intersection of their respective capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:86
msgid ""
"``Supported configurations`` are all configurations defined by the ``Common "
"link capabilities``' link rates and maximum lane count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:89
msgid ""
"``Disabled configurations`` are ``Supported configurations`` disabled via "
"this API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:92
msgid ""
"``Enabled configurations`` are ``Supported configurations`` that are not "
"disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:95
msgid ""
"``Forced configurations`` are ``Enabled configurations`` forced via forced "
"link parameter debugfs entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-capabilities:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_caps.c:98
msgid ""
"``Allowed configurations`` are the ``Enabled configurations``, or if forcing "
"is in effect the ``Forced configurations``, constrained by a maximum rate "
"and lane count set via the API."
msgstr ""

